This tool only takes `program_id`. Let me look at the other relevant tools to understand the full workflow, and also gather the necessary IDs. Let me check `list_programs`, `list_intakes`, `list_users`, and `list_rubrics`.

<tool_call>
{"name": "get_tool_detail_of", "arguments": {"tool_name": "list_programs"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_call>
{"name": "get_tool_detail_of", "arguments": {"tool_name": "list_intakes"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_call>
{"name": "get_tool_detail_of", "arguments": {"tool_name": "list_users"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_call>
{"name": "get_tool_detail_of", "arguments": {"tool_name": "list_rubrics"}}
</tool_call>

Now let me gather the necessary data: the Computer Science program, the Fall 2025 Undergraduate intake, the reviewer Priya Raman, and the rubric.

<tool_call>
{"name": "call_tool", "arguments": {"tool_name": "list_programs", "arguments": "{\"department\": \"Computer Science\"}"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_call>
{"name": "call_tool", "arguments": {"tool_name": "list_intakes", "arguments": "{\"term\": \"Fall\", \"year\": \"2025\", \"level\": \"Undergraduate\"}"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_call>
{"name": "call_tool", "arguments": {"tool_name": "list_users", "arguments": "{\"full_name\": \"Priya Raman\"}"}}
</tool_call>
<tool_call>
{"name": "call_tool", "arguments": {"tool_name": "list_rubrics", "arguments": "{\"name\": \"Undergraduate Holistic Review v3\"}"}}
</tool_call>
